The output-wide cases did reach the audit’s R3 regime and selected Triton kernels with 64-bit size arguments, so their passing results contradict the R3 store-overflow prediction. Two claims need narrowing: the real trunk was never run unguarded at exactly L or with backward, and `run_ppo` currently rejects the Kaggriculture model for trunk compilation.


